# Cursor Rules for Valkku Frontend

## Vue.js Development Rules

### Always Use Options API
- **MANDATORY**: Always use Vue.js Options API syntax, never Composition API
- Allow for setup()
- Use `export default { data(), methods: {}, computed: {}, etc. }` format
- Do NOT use `<script setup>` or Composition API syntax
- Do NOT use `ref()`, `reactive()`, `computed()`, or other Composition API functions
- Use `this.$` for accessing Vue instance properties and methods

### Code Style
- Use TypeScript for script blocks: `<script lang="ts">`
- Follow Vue 3 Options API patterns
- Use Vuetify components and styling
- Maintain consistent indentation and formatting
- Use self-closing tags when possible: `<v-radio />` instead of `<v-radio></v-radio>`
- Put attributes on separate lines when there are 2 or more: `<v-card variant="outlined" class="mb-4">` becomes multiple lines
- Use 2 spaces for indentation inside script blocks (ESLint vue/script-indent rule)

### Project Structure
- Components go in `src/components/`
- Pages go in `src/pages/`
- Use manual Vue Router configuration (no auto-routes)
- Use Vue I18n for internationalization
- Use Auth0 for authentication

### Examples of Correct Syntax:
```vue
<script lang="ts">
export default {
  name: 'ComponentName',
  data() {
    return {
      // reactive data
    }
  },
  computed: {
    // computed properties
  },
  methods: {
    // methods
  }
}
</script>
```

### Examples of INCORRECT Syntax (DO NOT USE):
```vue
<script setup>
// Composition API - FORBIDDEN
const data = ref()
const method = () => {}
</script>
```
